rylo odinga says he won't accept the  results of kenya's presidential election  he came second with 48  of the votes we have  beaten by then deputy president william  ruto with 50.7 percent  but he called the final tally a travesty  that can plunge the country into a legal  crisis  he blames the chair of the electoral  commission mafula chabukati our view in  this emilio is clear  the figures announced by mr buccati are  null and appointed  i repeat the figures and announcements  of publication are null and void and  must be crushed by a court of law  in our view  there is neither a legally and validly  declared winner not a president-elect  chaos broke out at the talling center  when some people tried to stop the  process  four out of seven commissioners walked  out in protests they say the  commission's chairman declared results  that they had not fully agreed on they  also said the total percentage of the  four presidential candidates did not add  up we concluded that  the process  that went into generation of  form 34c  which  he used to declare results of the  presidential election was opaque  and incapable of earning our ownership  and confidence  political coalition says it's compiling  a list of electoral malpractices that  went against the law rylo dinga and his  supporters say they will go to court  they have raised concerns about the  integrity of the presidential tally they  also say they have enough evidence to  support their case  members  they have seven days to file a petition  at the supreme court the judges will  then sit within 14 days to make a  decision catherine soy al jazeera  nairobi
 

